---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import AuthorTodo from '../components/AuthorTodo.astro';
---
<Base title="About — Katie Knox" section="about">
  <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

  <AuthorTodo note="Write the bio. Two or three paragraphs: what you work on, how you came to it, and what you are looking for next." />

  <div class="prose">
    <p class="todo">Bio needed.</p>

    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>
      Master of City Planning, University of Pennsylvania (2025–2027), Smart City
      concentration with a focus on urban spatial analysis. BA, Swarthmore College
      (2017–2022).
    </p>
    <p>
      Data &amp; Research Manager at the National Digital Inclusion Alliance since
      2022, working on program evaluation and research for national digital
      inclusion programmes.
    </p>

    <h2>A note on names</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses <b>Katie Knox</b>. Published writing for the National Digital
      Inclusion Alliance is bylined <b>Katie Knox Mimoune</b>, and the CV of record
      reads <b>Katherine Knox</b>.
    </p>

    <AuthorTodo note="Decide the display name for the site and replace the Katie Knox token in the layout and page titles." />

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <AuthorTodo note="Decide which contact details the site should carry. The CV currently lists a personal email address." />
    <p class="todo">Contact details needed.</p>

    <h2>CV</h2>
    <p>
      The full CV is on this site as a page — education, experience, skills and
      papers — at <a href="/cv">/cv</a>, with a
      <a href="/cv/katie-knox-cv.pdf">PDF version</a> generated from it.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .page-title { font-size: var(--step-3); margin: 0 0 var(--s-5); letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .prose { max-width: var(--measure); }
  .prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--face-mono); font-size: var(--step--1); font-weight: 400;
    text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: var(--ink-faint);
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--rule); padding-bottom: var(--s-2);
    margin: var(--s-7) 0 var(--s-4);
  }
  .prose p { margin: 0 0 var(--s-4); }
</style>
